paragraphs:
May your name be despised
for your conduct toward ladies,
from London to England,
from Seville to Cadiz;
may your cards bring no luck,
may your hand never trace
a king, a seven, or an ace
when you sit down to primera;
when your corns are pared,
may the knife cut to the quick;
and when your molars are pulled,
may the roots of them stick.
Bireno, Æneas — what worse name can I call you?
May Barabbas go with you! May every evil befall you!
